<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine cash wheat quiet on U.S. market holiday.</title>
<headline>Argentine cash wheat quiet on U.S. market holiday.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine wheat was slightly higher Monday in directionless trade because of the closure of U.S. markets for Presidents Day.</p>
<p>Traders said activity at Buenos Aires Cereals Exchange was thin.</p>
<p>Prices for wheat paid to farmers in Bahia Blanca rose $1 to $135. Buenos Aires April maize was up $3 at 104. April sunflower was flat at 198.</p>
<p>((--Buenos Aires Newsroom, +541 318-0668))</p>
